0.837066,"d":1319,"h":"Mo-Su 08:30-21:30","ad":"McLachlan Street","wifi":1},{"n":"Fort Hill (Darwin)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.469193,"lo":130.844904,"d":23,"ds":"Fort Hill is a hill that once existed on Darwin Harbour in the Northern Territory of Australia. It was the location of George Goyder's survey camp which was established in 1869.","wpu":"Fort Hill (Darwin)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Fort_Hill_1870.jpg/960px-Fort_Hill_1870.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Damoe-Ra Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.467083,"lo":130.842083,"d":381,"ds":"Damoe-Ra Park is an urban park in Darwin, Northern Territory, designated in 1996. The park was named Damoe-Ra because the park includes a spring sacred to the Larrakia women, and Damoe-Ra is the Larrakia word meaning \"eye\" or \"spring\". The park is situated below the escarpment on the coast below the Parliament House.","wpu":"Damoe-Ra Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Damoe_Ra_Pathway_Darwin_P5271413.jpg/960px-Damoe_Ra_Pathway_Darwin_P5271413.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bombing of Darwin","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.475,"lo":130.85,"d":860,"ds":"On 19 February 1942, 188 Japanese aircraft, in two separate raids, bombed the Australian town of Darwin, ships in Darwin Harbour and the town's two airfields in an attempt to prevent the Allies from using them as bases to contest the invasion of Timor and Java during World War II. This was the largest single attack ever mounted by a foreign power on Australia.","wpu":"Bombing of Darwin","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Darwin_42.jpg/960px-Darwin_42.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bicentennial Park (Darwin)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.460945,"lo":130.837061,"d":1243,"ds":"Bicentennial Park is a large area of parkland located in the Darwin city centre, Darwin, Northern Territory. It runs the length of Darwin's waterfront which looks over Darwin Harbour. The park stretches from Northern Territory Parliament House to Doctor's Gully.","wpu":"Bicentennial Park (Darwin)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/BicentennialParkDarwinOct172024_01.jpg/960px-BicentennialParkDarwinOct172024_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Stuart Park, Northern Territory","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.448611,"lo":130.841667,"d":2295,"ds":"Stuart Park is an inner suburb of the city of Darwin, Northern Territory, Australia. It is the traditional country and waterways of the Larrakia people.","wpu":"Stuart Park, Northern Territory","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Stuart-park-nt.jpg/960px-Stuart-park-nt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tiwi Islands Region","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.45,"lo":130.833,"d":2482,"ds":"The Tiwi Islands Region is a local government area (LGA) of the Northern Territory, Australia. The LGA covers an area of 7,483 square kilometres (2,889 sq mi) and had an estimated population of 2,753 in June 2018, and is governed by the Tiwi Islands Regional Council, formerly Tiwi Islands Shire Council.","wpu":"Tiwi Islands Region","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/66/Tiwi_Islands_Shire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"George Brown Darwin Botanic Gardens","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.445,"lo":130.836389,"d":2827,"ds":"The George Brown Darwin Botanic Gardens is a botanical garden located 2 km north of the CBD of Darwin, Northern Territory, Australia.","wpu":"George Brown Darwin Botanic Gardens","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Darwin_Bontanic_Gardens.jpg/960px-Darwin_Bontanic_Gardens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bayview, Northern Territory","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.440312,"lo":130.860162,"d":3589,"ds":"Bayview is an upper middle class inner city suburb of Darwin, Northern Territory, Australia. It is bounded by Tiger Brennan Drive, the bay area and the Charles Darwin National Park. It is in the local government area of the City of Darwin.","wpu":"Bayview, Northern Territory","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Bayview_nt.jpg/960px-Bayview_nt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Darwin Pioneer Cemetery","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.43697,"lo":130.8406,"d":3593,"ds":"Darwin Pioneer Cemetery was the first official cemetery opened in Darwin in the Northern Territory of Australia. It was originally known as Palmerston Cemetery. The cemetery stands as a testament to the many different cultural groups with different religious affiliations that lived in the early years of the city.","wpu":"Darwin Pioneer Cemetery","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Pioneer_Cemetery_Darwin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Charles Darwin National Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.450833,"lo":130.873333,"d":3680,"ds":"Charles Darwin National Park is a national park in the Northern Territory of Australia, 4 km southeast of Darwin. It is notable for its World War II–era concrete bunkers, one of which has been converted into a visitors centre and display of World War II memorabilia. It also has lookouts towards the city of Darwin.","wpu":"Charles Darwin National Park","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cc/CDNP_lookout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Darwin ( DAR-win; Larrakia: Garramilla) is the capital and largest city of the Northern Territory, Australia. The city had a population of 139,902 at the 2021 census, which is nearly 63% of the territory's population. It is the smallest, wettest, and most northerly of the Australian capital cities and serves as the Top End's regional centre.","wpu":"Darwin, Northern Territory","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/DarwinOct172024_02.jpg/960px-DarwinOct172024_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}